<PageLayout title="Help me see what you’re seeing."><main id="main" class="resource-main"><a class="text-link" href="/resources/">← Back to resources</a><p class="eyebrow">SUPPORT / <Wordmark inline/> JOURNAL</p><h1>Help me see what you’re seeing.</h1><p>A useful support request describes the problem and how to reach it. You don’t need to know the technical cause.</p><h2>Start with the change</h2><p>Tell me what you expected, what happened instead, and when you first noticed it. Name the website, device, or service involved.</p><h2>List the steps</h2><p>For example: “I open the services page, select the request button, and the form doesn’t appear.” Include your browser and whether you’re using a phone or a computer when it’s relevant.</p><h2>Explain the impact</h2><p>Let me know whether it is a question, an inconvenience, or something preventing you from working. Mention any recent changes that might provide context.</p><h2>Keep private details private</h2><p>Don’t send passwords, card details, or confidential documents in an initial message. Ask for an appropriate way to share files if they are needed.</p><a class="button" href="/support/">Prepare a support request →</a></main></PageLayout>